We started in the digital realm of AI prompts, looking at the strict math of continuation operators.

41:24.180 --> 41:28.280
We learned that static operators, those fixed rules, don't care about order.

41:28.280 --> 41:33.660
We discovered the absolute chaos of the override, which just throws history in the trash.

41:34.040 --> 41:42.500
We exposed the quiet trickery of state-dependent operators, which changed their meaning based on the present moment, slicing the space relative to what's already there.

41:42.740 --> 41:48.440
And we felt the unbreakable gravity of persistent operators, the system rules we just can't escape.

41:49.000 --> 41:55.440
From there, we played detective with information forensics, realizing that while overrides destroy history entirely,

41:55.440 --> 41:59.300
state-dependent operators lock history away inside a paradox.

41:59.620 --> 42:03.340
They freeze dynamic choices into static rules that hide their own origins.

